# arch/os/windows — Windows process services.
#
# The counterpart of arch/os/linux and arch/os/macos, directory for directory
# where Windows has an answer:
#
#   io/      the calls a program makes when there is no C library under it to
#            make them through — kernel32, ntdll and Winsock, because on
#            Windows the system call numbers are ntdll's and change with every
#            build, so the instruction is not a thing a program may make.
#
#   entropy/ BCryptGenRandom() the same freestanding way, beside io/ and for
#            the same reason: the one call a program draws randomness with, and
#            the seam a reader of it rides.
#
#   scan/    pure functions over a run of code: where the system call
#            instructions in it are — on Windows, in ntdll's stubs.
#
#   include/ not built: the POSIX headers Windows does not have, answered over
#            the Windows API so that sources which include them compile
#            unchanged. kbuild puts it on the include path of every Windows
#            compile (scripts/Makefile.shared).
#
# There is no sc/ here yet; README.md says what it would take.
#
# PLATFORM is not a Kconfig symbol. kbuild derives it from the target triple
# before the configuration is read — x86_64-w64-mingw32, aarch64-w64-mingw32 and
# clang's *-windows-gnu all name this directory — and every tool and test
# compile force-includes arch/os/$(PLATFORM)/platform.h, which is empty here and
# is only ever the file that has to exist.
obj-$(CONFIG_OS_IO)      += io/
obj-$(CONFIG_OS_ENTROPY) += entropy/
obj-$(CONFIG_OS_SCAN)    += scan/
